.TXT 2 1 19 0
Cg a72.500000,73.000000,322
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {\b FIRexa.mcd}  to show the frequency
 response of two subband filters used for
 data compression in a prototype portable
 video-on-demand wireless receiver. (Low
 power was the dominant design consideration.
 Meng, et.al., "Portable video-on-demand
 in wireless communication", Proc IEEE 83,
 No 4, April 1995, pp. 659-680.}
}
.TXT 11 0 68 0
Cg a23.250000,73.000000,34
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {\b \fs24 Background Information}}
}
.TXT 4 5 69 0
Cg a63.375000,68.000000,133
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {\ul System} Design Criteria: (i)
 low power consumption; (ii) high compression
 efficiency; (iii) channel error resiliency.
 [p. 659]}
}
.TXT 7 0 70 0
Cg a63.500000,68.000000,87
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain Compression Algorithm: lattice vector
 quantization and subband decomposition.
 [p. 663]}
}
.TXT 5 0 72 0
Cg a24.125000,68.000000,32
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain Subband Decomposition: [p. 663]}
}
.TXT 4 4 74 0
Cg a53.000000,64.000000,155
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain Advantages: (i) no "block" artifacts;
 (ii) hierarchical nature implies flexible
 quantization/bit-allocation; (iii) architectural
 tradeoffs for low power.}
}
.TXT 8 0 75 0
Cg a63.125000,64.000000,133
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain Algorithm structure: uses multiple
 stages of subband decomposition; use fixed
 low and high pass filters with interspersed
 sampling.}
}
.TXT 7 0 76 0
Cg a50.500000,64.000000,79
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {\ul Filter} Design Criteria: additionally
 want accurate reproduction of image}
}
.TXT 5 0 77 0
Cg a62.750000,64.000000,231
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain Candidate Types: (i) Quadrature 
Mirror Filters: near-perfect reconstruction;
 (ii) wavelet filters: near perfect magnitude
 reconstruction but nonlinear phase; (iii)
 "short" FIR filter: see attached excerpt
 for tradeoffs [p. 673].}
}
